    "\n",
    "Answer: \n",
    "    We decided to investigate the following features for further examination, taxvaluedollarcnt, lotsizesquarefeet,  bedroomcnt, and yearbuilt. For taxvaluedollarcnt (the target variable), we found that the histogram exhibited a highly right-skewed distribution, with most properties clustered at lower tax values and a small number of extreme outliers above 10 million. The lotsizesquarefeet feature also showed a heavily skewed distribution with extreme outliers that could distort model training later on. Bedroomcnt appears to be a unimodal distribution with most homes having between 2 and 4 bedrooms. Finally, yearbuilt shows clusters of constructuin activitry with a stark increase after 1950. These features were initially chosen because these characteristics often contribute the most to the price of a home but this will need to be validated later in the correlation matrix. Overall, these observations highlighted the need for carful treatment of outliers since there are extreme values for both sides of the sprectrum. "
