    "#### **3.D Discussion:**  Describe in a paragraph your decisions about which methods you used to impute missing values in the dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer: We used different imputation strategies for numerical and categorical features based on what was most applicable for the given situation. For numerical columns, we applied median imputation because many of these features, such as lotsizesquarefeet and taxvaluedollarcnt, have skewed distributions and potential outliers. Median values tend to preserve the central tendency of the data without distorting it as opposed to outlier values. For categorical features, we used mode imputation, replacing missing values with the most frequent category in each column. This was done to try and maintain the consistency for the data. Together, these methods were implemented to try and ensure that no missing values remained while minimizing the risk of introducing bias or noise into the dataset.\n"
   ]
